I agree with you Tim and I'll forward it to the list.  I had second
thoughts as I was writing it yesterday because I was doing it quickly. I
tried to make it clear that much of this was under the user's control
and would depend on whether they kept L constant or not.  Your argument
assumes constant L.  The point I was making was that we use the
log-normal distribution because of the skewed nature of the data and
because the estimated se is often proportional to the estimated
abundance (constant cv). But that is a sampling issue with regard to a
constant density not a varying one. Your point is a good one and she
might consider using the inverse scenario if they presume that they keep
L constant.

